currently, I can run most things concurrently. though, every once in a while, we need to lock down the mutex and save or load stuff. this blocks completely unrelated threads from running. for instance, assume app A, app B and app C exist. Now assumeapp A and app B, and app A and app C are in communication with one another. now, app A instanciates two thread info structs that live right next to each other that never change size. Now, if B sends data to A, and A tries to store it in thread info, A will lock its mutex to prevent any new process from communicating with A thus instanciating a new thread info struct thus reallocating the pointer potentially rendering the pointers of A->B and A->C invalid thus segfaulting. However, if both B and C send A data at the same (or similar) time, A will still lock to one process and first write one message, then the other, though due to the constant
